A solid 30-second answer to:

“Future vs Queueable?”

> Both execute work asynchronously, but for new development I generally prefer Queueable because it provides a job ID, supports richer state and allows job chaining. Future methods are simpler and commonly found in legacy implementations, but have more restrictive parameter handling and less control.




