4. Git/GitHub + Harness — Rebase & Deployment | ~10 min

Yesterday: merge conflict.

Today: rebase.

Imagine:

main

A──B──C

feature

A──B──D──E

Meanwhile main gets C.

You run:

git checkout feature/SF-1023
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main

Git conceptually rewrites your feature commits on top of latest main:

A──B──C──D'──E'

Important:

Rebase rewrites commit history.

Therefore be careful rebasing branches other developers are already using.

Interview question:

Merge vs rebase?

Good answer:

> Merge combines histories and creates a merge commit when necessary, preserving branch history. Rebase reapplies commits on top of another base and can create a cleaner linear history, but because it rewrites commit history I avoid casually rebasing shared branches.



